  "findings": [
    "The pointwise next theorem applies the correct converse from an empty oriented arc to the actual nextGaussVisit. It supplies distinctness of the actual incoming and return newborn visits, derived from disjoint old/new labels, and the complete no-between statement for every actual child visit. It proves incoming-next=return, not merely symmetric adjacency or absence of a selected subset of visits.",
    "The converse dependency uses the canonical sorted finite visit order and handles the last/first cut explicitly. It requires distinct endpoints but no minimum of three visits. Its four preserved consumers check both forward and wrap successors for two- and three-member finite sets. Therefore a parent with no crossings and a loop child with only the two newborn visits remains covered.",
    "The combined theorem uses the full n>=3, parent Generic, arbitrary j and SoftAdmissible domain. It obtains positive word and arc radii, takes their strictly positive minimum, and specializes both results to the same epsilon with the two explicit min inequalities. It neither equates the two radii nor assumes either theorem at epsilon zero.",
    "At that fixed P,j,q,epsilon, hQ and hQ′ both prove exactly Generic(softInsertion P j q epsilon); hp and hp′ both prove exactly SoftCrossingPersistence P j q epsilon; hclass and hclass′ both prove exactly SoftCrossingClassificationAt P j q epsilon. Each of these is Prop. Lean proof irrelevance therefore aligns only proofs of identical propositions, including their proof-dependent projections. No arbitrary polygon, edge map, crossing support, parameter, radius, order or other Type-valued datum is identified.",
    "The inherited crossing and visit constructions already have fixed support/edge data from the physical map; their hp arguments only certify the resulting crossing propositions. The newborn crossing and visit data are likewise the fixed incoming/return support and member edges; hclass and hloop certify their validity. Thus passing arc bounds from the primed witnesses to the unprimed witnesses does not replace actual correspondence data.",
    "Under each loop proof, derived child G1 gives strict (0,1) canonical parameters for the two actual newborn visits. The physical-path theorem supplies incoming successor=old attachment and soft-edge successor=return, together with exact vertex evaluations Pj and Pj+epsilon*q. This retains the source path through both vertices, arbitrary insertion position and residue-zero wrap.",
    "The arc conclusion quantifies over every actual child Visit. The dependency proof exhausts a child visit as one of the two newborn endpoints or as inherited, excludes endpoints by strict cyclic order, and excludes each inherited visit by the proved incoming/return parameter windows and physical ParentArc arithmetic. It does not assume the empty arc or overlook soft-edge visits, which cannot occur by the crossing classification.",
    "The first theorem then converts these derived bounds and the complete empty arc into the actual nextGaussVisit equality. The final tuple also retains the already proved Cycle deletion and crossing-word deletion on the same interval, with the same actual newborn crossing and inherited maps. Filtering preserves repetitions when visits are mapped to crossing letters.",
    "For the non-loop sector, the same interval retains the mapped parent gaussWord equality from the word transport theorem. Empty parent lists are supported by the sorted-list and Cycle proofs, with no selected crossing or nonempty-cycle premise. Loop and non-loop conclusions use their explicit source sector conditions.",
    "All 26 complete embedded bodies match exactly once and in the declared order. The original drafts equal the first successful root31945 files. Both own axiom traces are standard foundational axioms; all 25 predecessor receipts and their bound files were verified. NewbornVisits13 and Next3 plus its four consumers were inspected through their full proof interfaces and preserved evidence. No implementation or source file was changed."
